     ccllnntt__ppeerrrrnnoo()
            Print a message to standard error corresponding to the condition
            indicated by _s_t_a_t.  A newline is appended.  Normally used after a
            procedure call fails for a routine for which a client handle is
            not needed, for instance rrppcc__ccaallll().

     ccllnntt__ppeerrrroorr()
            Print a message to the standard error indicating why an RPC call
            failed; _c_l_n_t is the handle used to do the call.  The message is
            prepended with string _s and a colon.  A newline is appended.  Nor‐
            mally used after a remote procedure call fails for a routine which
            requires a client handle, for instance ccllnntt__ccaallll().

     ccllnntt__ssppeerrrrnnoo()
            Take the same arguments as ccllnntt__ppeerrrrnnoo(), but instead of sending a
            message to the standard error indicating why an RPC call failed,
