            when the program does not have a standard error (as a program run‐
            ning as a server quite likely does not), or if the programmer does
            not want the message to be output with pprriinnttff() (see printf(3)),
            or if a message format different than that supported by
            ccllnntt__ppeerrrrnnoo() is to be used.  Note: unlike ccllnntt__ssppeerrrroorr() and
            ccllnntt__ssppccrreeaatteeeerrrroorr() (see rpc_clnt_create(3)), ccllnntt__ssppeerrrrnnoo() does
